WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:00.800
Your project

00:00:00.800 --> 00:00:01.520
has grown,

00:00:01.520 --> 00:00:01.840
and the

00:00:01.840 --> 00:00:02.640
guide belongs

00:00:02.640 --> 00:00:04.000
with the documentation.

00:00:04.000 --> 00:00:05.040
Moving it should

00:00:05.040 --> 00:00:05.600
change where

00:00:05.600 --> 00:00:06.160
people find

00:00:06.160 --> 00:00:06.480
it,

00:00:06.480 --> 00:00:07.200
while keeping

00:00:07.200 --> 00:00:07.600
the same

00:00:07.600 --> 00:00:08.600
useful content.

00:00:10.500 --> 00:00:10.980
The move

00:00:10.980 --> 00:00:11.540
command is

00:00:11.540 --> 00:00:12.180
a convenience

00:00:12.180 --> 00:00:13.700
for that reorganization.

00:00:13.700 --> 00:00:14.180
It moves

00:00:14.180 --> 00:00:14.740
the file

00:00:14.740 --> 00:00:15.060
to its

00:00:15.060 --> 00:00:15.780
new path

00:00:15.780 --> 00:00:16.820
and stages the

00:00:16.820 --> 00:00:17.460
result.

00:00:17.460 --> 00:00:18.020
The move

00:00:18.020 --> 00:00:18.500
still needs

00:00:18.500 --> 00:00:19.260
a commit.

00:00:21.000 --> 00:00:21.400
Here is

00:00:21.400 --> 00:00:22.440
the subtle part.

00:00:22.440 --> 00:00:22.840
It does

00:00:22.840 --> 00:00:23.320
not save

00:00:23.320 --> 00:00:24.360
a special permanent

00:00:24.360 --> 00:00:25.560
rename event.

00:00:25.560 --> 00:00:27.320
When comparing snapshots,

00:00:27.320 --> 00:00:27.640
it can

00:00:27.640 --> 00:00:28.760
recognize a rename

00:00:28.760 --> 00:00:29.480
from matching

00:00:29.480 --> 00:00:30.720
or similar content.

00:00:33.160 --> 00:00:33.720
So think

00:00:33.720 --> 00:00:33.960
of the

00:00:33.960 --> 00:00:34.600
result.

00:00:34.600 --> 00:00:35.080
The old

00:00:35.080 --> 00:00:35.560
path is

00:00:35.560 --> 00:00:36.040
gone.

00:00:36.040 --> 00:00:36.440
The new

00:00:36.440 --> 00:00:37.240
path contains

00:00:37.240 --> 00:00:37.960
the guide,

00:00:37.960 --> 00:00:38.440
and that

00:00:38.440 --> 00:00:39.720
change is staged.

00:00:39.720 --> 00:00:40.920
A rename label

00:00:40.920 --> 00:00:42.280
describes the comparison.

00:00:42.280 --> 00:00:43.400
A commit records

00:00:43.400 --> 00:00:44.920
the prepared snapshot.

00:00:44.920 --> 00:00:46.920
Content similarity and comparison

00:00:46.920 --> 00:00:47.560
settings can

00:00:47.560 --> 00:00:48.040
affect that

00:00:48.040 --> 00:00:49.040
rename label.
